ha, they set about creating the worlds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.812,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-63-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7055011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce4a2c2cafb5a33ab5be47c8a957be5f77c6c8d6d01edc2ceec631082fc5d85c","compact":"dba84a449268f39220df5a65bbcca207c536c2f8f1f0f8917c6ea0a7dbeebd56","nasal":"dba84a449268f39220df5a65bbcca207c536c2f8f1f0f8917c6ea0a7dbeebd56"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-55-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":55,"verse":12,"english":"O Kākutstha, this shaft was forged when invisible by celestials and Asuras the divine selfsprung and invincible (deity) reposed on the mighty main, and when creation was oppressed by Madhu and Kaitabha as well as other Räks asas. He, overwhelmed with rage desirous of creating the three worlds, created the best of arrows invincible to all beings, for the extraction of the wicked ones; and destroyed them in battle by means of this very arrow. And having with this foremost of shafts finished Madhu and Kait abha, they set about creating the worlds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-63-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7055012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8419dc97eb0ff13adcc0256fd1e97ea3e65059383d6ca932ee180d37daa0767a","compact":"fdd40806eee3724c26fe6bea0811724ce99d4f75aec891a9f8eeef68526c66fd","nasal":"fdd40806eee3724c26fe6bea0811724ce99d4f75aec891a9f8eeef68526c66fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-55-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":55,"verse":13,"english":"When, O Satrughna, formerly I sought to slay Råvaņa, I did not discharge this arrow, thinking that if discharged, it would inflict great havoc on creatures.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.677,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-63-